atio of shared bias to idiosyncratic variance. Compared to a single expert, the panel wins when the expert's idiosyncratic noise (unreliable intuition) exceeds the checklist's systematic bias. The expert wins when the checklist's bias exceeds the expert's noise. 'Mere checklist compliance tracking the right answer' is the degenerate case where the checklist bias is zero and noise is zero\u2014perfect reliability but no generalization. The genuine gain is when the checklist bias is small and noise cancels, yielding high accuracy the expert cannot achieve due to their own volatility.","premises":[],"schema":"deepreason-reasoning-envelope-v1","scope":{"covers":[],"excludes":[]},"simulation_refs":[],"uncertainties":[]}
